Template: tergite-mss/database
Type: select
Choices-C: postgresql, mongodb, url
Choices: local PostgreSQL, local MongoDB, existing database
Default: postgresql
Description: Database for MSS:
 A local database gets its own tergite-mss account, created on the service's
 first start. PostgreSQL comes with this package; MongoDB has to be installed
 from mongodb.org.

Template: tergite-mss/database_url
Type: string
Description: URL of the existing database, without its password:
 With its user, e.g. postgresql+asyncpg://mss@db.example.com:5432/mss or
 mongodb://mss@db.example.com:27017/mss. The password is asked next.

Template: tergite-mss/database_password
Type: password
Description: Password of the database user:
 Stored only in /etc/tergite-mss/mss-config.toml, which root and the
 tergite-mss service alone can read. Leave it empty if the user has none.
